{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat in Vienna is a trial. I spent the morning at Prince Lichtenstein’s gallery until noon, where the light was better than the crowd. Then I took the carriage to Währing, half an hour out, to see Rembold. He is a decent man, though his philosophy is mostly dust. We crossed the Danube arm to lunch in the Augarten. The fish was acceptable, costing me two florins, but the wine was thin.\n\nI walked the Prater, which is merely trees and noise, then caught the Leopoldstadt theatre. Schuster played the Magister; he is loud and wooden. The farce, *Die Zauberbirn*, followed. It was vulgar, but the audience loved it. I paid a gulden for the seat.\n\nKarl’s letter arrived yesterday; he is well, though his arithmetic remains slow. I shall send the books I promised when I return.\n\nYour affectionate,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219055,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":207,"prompt_tokens":1128,"total_tokens":1335,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-4icUg7k6OiEYRXXKvJ4k9yOWyByHsNQu","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1128,"prompt_ms":1084.179,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9611515957446809,"prompt_per_second":1040.4186024632463,"predicted_n":207,"predicted_ms":4849.375,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.540655339805824,"predicted_per_second":42.47970099239593}}